<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Prim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1814">1814</a>–<a href="/years/1870">1870</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Juan Prim y Prats</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Prim was a Spanish general and Liberal politician who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution-spain">Glorious Revolution</a> of 1868 that overthrew Isabella II. As head of government he searched <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> for a new king, a search that helped spark the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-prussian-war">Franco-Prussian War</a>, and secured the election of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amadeo-i-of-spain">Amadeo of Savoy</a>. He was shot in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a> in December 1870 and died days later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-prim.jpg" alt="Juan Prim" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antonio María Esquivel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antonio_Mar%C3%ADa_Esquivel_-_El_General_Prim.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
